From 579b155a8c6d278af9b91e436393f4da700dae2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Jezl <john@jezl.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:01:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] V1 (#1216 experiment): idle WFE so the push SEV wakes idle
 thieves

H3 for #1216 says idle CPUs sleep in WFI, smp_notify_cpu() is SEV only,
and SEV does not end WFI, so an idle thief on Jetson wakes only on its
own 100 Hz tick. This changes the one idle wait compiled on Pi 5 and on
Jetson with JETSON_HW_TICK (the SECONDARY_PREEMPT branch of
idle_task_func) from WFI to WFE. WFE ends on SEV and on every interrupt
that ends WFI, so the change only adds wake events. The other idle-loop
wait branches are mutually exclusive preprocessor alternatives for
other configurations and are unchanged; QEMU builds compile none of
them.

Experiment commit for cells B and G of coherency run 3, not for merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/sched/sched.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/sched.c b/kernel/sched/sched.c
index e3a29e12..ffcd92ff 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.c
@@ -655,10 +655,14 @@ static void idle_task_func(void *arg)
          * tools/tfa-patches/0004-*. Both: per-CPU CNTHP fires Group
          * 1 NS IRQs at NS-EL2/VHE; daifclr unmasks I, WFI sleeps
          * until the next tick. The ELR trampoline handles the
-         * switch_to-in-ISR problem on secondary CPUs. */
+         * switch_to-in-ISR problem on secondary CPUs.
+         *
+         * V1 (#1216 experiment): WFE instead of WFI, so the SEV that
+         * smp_notify_cpu() already issues on every push wakes idle
+         * thieves; WFE also wakes on every interrupt WFI wakes on. */
         __asm__ volatile("msr daifclr, #2" ::: "memory");
         __asm__ volatile("isb" ::: "memory");
-        __asm__ volatile("wfi");
+        __asm__ volatile("wfe" ::: "memory");
 #elif defined(PLATFORM_JETSON_ORIN_NANO)
         /* Jetson without JETSON_HW_TICK (stock BL31): hardware timer
          * IRQs do not deliver to EL1/EL2 because the GIC group/route
